212
00:12:16,050 --> 00:12:20,650
The feature freeze is active and will remain in place until after the pilot review.

213
00:12:20,650 --> 00:12:23,710
Right, and I want to be very explicit.

214
00:12:23,710 --> 00:12:29,050
Any request that sounds small but requires code changes is still out of scope.

215
00:12:29,050 --> 00:12:33,730
If someone believes a change is critical, it must be escalated with a clear business

216
00:12:33,730 --> 00:12:37,690
case, impact assessment, and timing implications.

217
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:40,330
That level of discipline is necessary.

218
00:12:40,330 --> 00:12:43,810
Engineering teams perform best when priorities are stable.

219
00:12:43,810 --> 00:12:47,730
Constant context switching leads to quality issues, which is the opposite of what we want

220
00:12:47,730 --> 00:12:49,050
right now.

221
00:12:49,050 --> 00:12:50,050
Exactly.

222
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:52,690
